The problem asks us to find the number of undirected connected simple graphs with $N$ vertices (labeled 1 to $N$) and $M$ edges such that the number of vertices with an even shortest distance from vertex 1 is equal to the number of vertices with an odd shortest distance from vertex 1. We need to output this count modulo $P$ for all $M$ from $N-1$ to $\frac{N(N-1)}{2}$. The constraints are $N \le 30$ and $P$ is a large prime.

Let $d(v)$ be the shortest distance from vertex 1 to vertex $v$ in the graph.
The condition is $|\{v \mid d(v) \text{ is even}\}| = |\{v \mid d(v) \text{ is odd}\}|$.
